      "summary": "The revised block boundary addresses the prior column-zero brace case, but a block-like heredoc line can still truncate the locals scan and let an opaque credential reach an output undetected.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/release-identity.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 423,
          "message": "The locals scan can still truncate at a block-like line inside a heredoc, missing a later credential-bearing local and allowing an output to expose its opaque value.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The locals-block regex stops at any line beginning with a Terraform block keyword. It does not distinguish actual block declarations from heredoc content.",
            "failureScenario": "If a locals block has a heredoc containing a line such as `resource \"example\" {` before `hidden_key = azurerm_storage_account.demo.primary_access_key`, the regex truncates the locals block before `hidden_key`. An output referencing `local.hidden_key` has no credential-bearing expression for the source check to detect, and an opaque key can evade the evaluated-value pattern check. The test passes while an output exposes the storage key."
          }
        }
      ]
