          "line": 423,
          "message": "The block scan can stop inside a heredoc when its content begins a line with a Terraform block keyword, allowing a credential reference later in the output to escape AC RELEASE-ID-04.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The regex ends an output or locals block when it encounters a newline followed by a Terraform block keyword. Terraform heredoc strings can contain those lines, so the scan can stop inside a valid output value before checking its remaining contents.",
            "failureScenario": "If an existing output is changed to a heredoc containing a line beginning `resource ` followed by an interpolation of `azurerm_storage_account.demo.primary_access_key`, the scan truncates at `resource `. The output can expose the opaque key while the source scan and evaluated-value patterns pass, violating AC RELEASE-ID-04 (OWASP A02:2025 Security Misconfiguration)."
